00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.740
Dividend income strategies and tax advantage to counts like the TFSA reward predictable

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.660
cash flows from regulated assets.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.180
Enbridge fits this profile because 98% of its earnings come from regulated utilities

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.020
and long-term contracts, with 80% index to inflation.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.720
Investors can implement the approach by screening for companies that have raised dividends

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.880
for at least 30 consecutive years and maintain a payout ratio below 70%.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.660
The current 5.9% yield on Enbridge offers a concrete example of how inflation protected

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.820
cash flows compound tax-free inside a TFSA.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:08.180
This method performed well during the 2008 to 2009 downturn when commodity-exposed names

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.000
cut payouts while regulated pipelines held steady.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.840
The main risk is regulatory changes that cap allowed returns, which can compress multiples

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.860
even when cash flow remains stable.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.020
Canadian investors should verify the latest distribution coverage ratio on the company's

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.940
investor site before adding exposure.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:32.000
Enbridge has met or exceeded its financial guidance for 19 consecutive years, which supports

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.940
the reliability of those cash flows.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.080
The company operates more than 200 revenue generating assets across North America.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.520
Total shareholder return exceeds 855% over the past 20 years.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.900
Imagine you bought an ETF tracking small-cap Canadian names last week when volume was

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:50.180
thin.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.140
Your order filled at a price 3 cents above the previous close because the market maker

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.640
widened the spread to protect against low liquidity.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.200
The mechanism works through the difference between the highest bid and lowest offer.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:08.060
In calm markets, that gap might be 2 cents, but it can jump to 15 cents in the first 30

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:13.360
minutes of a volatile session. What most retail investors do not realize is that the spread

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:19.480
cost is paid on every round-trip trade, so a 1% annual fee plus repeated spreads can erase

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:25.220
the entire expected excess return over an index fund. The pro tip is to check the average

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.960
daily volume and the current bid-ass quote in your platform's order ticket before placing

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:36.060
a market order on any ETF under $50 million in assets. The concrete misconception to

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:42.440
avoid is assuming every ETF trades as tightly as the S&amp;P 500 trackers. Always compare the

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.220
spread to the management fee before committing capital. Broad market funds such as the

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.320
iShares S&amp;P TSX capped composite index ETF keep these costs lower because they attract

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.700
consistent liquidity. Hidden execution costs inside funds that use options can compound

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:04.500
the problem further. This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. Today's pick

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.340
is BlackBerry on the TSX under the tickerbb.to.

